{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Rule 6c-11:** An AP must be a member or participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency and have a written agreement with **the ETF or one of its service providers** permitting creation/redemption orders. The rule does not require the ETF itself to sign.\n\n**US agreement forms:** The principal signatories are commonly **the AP and the distributor**, sometimes with additional service providers. The trust may be expressly designated a **third-party beneficiary**, rather than a contracting signatory. I cannot confirm the particular “reviewed” forms without their identities.\n\n**Irish ICAV arrangement:** The ICAV itself typically contracts with the AP, potentially alongside its manager or other providers. Thus, the fund vehicle has direct contractual standing, rather than merely beneficiary status. The precise parties depend on the agreement.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Regulatory permission, contractual-party status, and third-party-beneficiary rights are distinct."}}
